      "explanation": "To find \\(f(\\tfrac12)\\), choose an input \\(x\\) for which \\(g(x)=\\tfrac12\\). Since \\(g(x)=1-x^2\\), we want \\(x^2=\\tfrac12\\). One permissible choice is \\(x=1/\\sqrt2\\), which is nonzero.\n\nSubstituting this input into the given identity yields\n\\[\nf\\left(\\frac12\\right)\n=\\frac{1-\\frac12}{\\frac12}=1.\n\\]\nThus the answer is \\(1\\), choice B.",
